{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1552995-lambda-gadget-creation-blade-of-water","id":1552995,"title":"Lambda Gadget Creation: Blade of Water","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-07T17:03:17-07:00","id":1552995,"title":"Lambda Gadget Creation: Blade of Water","content":"I have been running a long term game of Demon. We have a player creating a new character and joining the game late. Most of the characters in the game have been focused gun bunnies and had gadgets build or purchased to turn them into even more dangerous firearms wielder. However, this new character wants to use weapons and avoid firearms altogether if he can avoid it. To support this and because there is not merit to support starting Gadgets. I have decided to allow him to come in with a gadget weapon to be on par with the others in the group.<br /> <br /> I have decided to create a Tier 1 Lambda Gadget sword for him.<br /> <br /> I am looking to use the Embed Ripple and the Exploit Break The Dam as the basis of this gadget. I'm looking for a gadget sword hilt that when activated would gather the moisture in the air to form the blade of the weapon. When not active it looks like maybe an strange anime sword hilt. I think thematically, these fit but I am having trouble with a designing the mechanics. Would appreciate some suggestion.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27908-metalith","name":"metalith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T20:29:55-07:00","id":1552998,"title":"","content":"Without knowing what else you want this thing to be able to do, it sounds like making it a lambda might be overengineering the thing; a form gadget using the described water-based variant of the Laser Cutter form power would probably do the trick if all you need is a rationale for having a sword hilt that serves as a projected hydrocutter.<br /> <br /> If that's not workable, remember that regardless of the design process that gets you there and the breadth of functionality, a lambda is made out of multiple gadgets and can be no smaller than the largest of its components, and gadgets are by design more limited (and lateral, in the case of near-field effects) versions of their incorporated Embeds and Exploits. What gadgets that derive from Ripple and Break the Dam were used to make this thing? Were all its components made by the same demon? To what end were the pieces made and how did the PC come into the lambda? The answers to these questions may help connect the lambda and its bearer to the larger world in a way that also expands the story, especially if they can be linked to the character's answers to the Five Questions detailing potential sources of compromise.<br /> <br /> On a more practical level, while it's nice to have a niche to focus on, it's probably worth noting that if the character intends to focus on melee weaponry to the exclusion of firearms altogether then they are angling either much quieter or much more distinctive re: solving problems with violence, such that it's important to know if their intended playstyle would benefit from being handed an obviously unnatural weapon. In terms of the quadrants laid out in the Storyteller's Guide, is this player participating in a Smashing, Insurgent, Gritty, or Silent game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-08T00:59:42-07:00","id":1553004,"title":"","content":"The game is not set in a specific quadrant, it has been running for a moment and over time has shifted as the plot moves along. Most of the players have only had a passing experience with WW games, so for the first few story arc I would say we floated between Insurgent and Gritty. As they have gotten more comfortable with the game added more aspects and increased the scope of the game. The most recent story is taking the game in a more Smashing direction since due to the scope of the story events. I kind of wanted to tell a Burn Notice kind of style game, where violence is needed it is not hidden and when stealth is needed its there.<br /> <br /> I decided on a Lambda due to the Multi-Tool one being very nice but the weapon options did not fit his aesthetic. He is a blade weapon user. After discussing with him, his character has no skills nor interest in crafts or has an goal towards that. So looking to create something based of that. Form gadgets have the draw back if the demon dies or other flaws can destroy the Form Gadget in question.<br /> <br /> I have not designed the specifics of the lower level gadgets yet. I am thinking that they would be weapon based gadgets as well. As far as the creator, I am thinking that creator of the lambda may have created one of the lower lever gadgets. I have been seeding the idea of a master demon gadgeteer. One player was successful with creation of his exploited Hell Fire Rifle but it lead to some trouble.<br /> <br /> Tentative ideas<br /> <br /> Ripple : Resonant Dagger - A lethal sonic dagger that cuts like a chainsaw. Which triggers its ripple effect on the damaged caused with the dagger only.<br /> Break the Dam : Vampiric Tongue - A short sword that hungers for the blood, when triggers inflicts additional damage by sucking out the blood.<br /> <br /> I have not gone into the details with the play since we still have 2 weeks before our next game and he will start playing that game. But I did tell him I would be giving him a starting gadget to go with his character since other player have either made their own or traded for gadgets.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27908-metalith","name":"metalith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-08T15:32:35-07:00","id":1553017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>metalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1552995-lambda-gadget-creation-blade-of-water?p=1553004#post1553004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> decided on a Lambda due to the Multi-Tool one being very nice but the weapon options did not fit his aesthetic. He is a blade weapon user. After discussing with him, his character has no skills nor interest in crafts or has an goal towards that. So looking to create something based of that. Form gadgets have the draw back if the demon dies or other flaws can destroy the Form Gadget in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting that, unless I'm forgetting something from another book, Flowers' section on form gadgets simply says that nobody knows what happens to a form gadget whose originating demon dies, but point taken.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you mean by the weapon options of the Infinite Multitool not fitting the character's aesthetic \u2014 the mechanical results have the same Damage/Initiative profile as a standard machete and reskinning is one of the easier ways to modify existing published items. What kind of aesthetics is the character working with?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have not designed the specifics of the lower level gadgets yet. I am thinking that they would be weapon based gadgets as well. As far as the creator, I am thinking that creator of the lambda may have created one of the lower lever gadgets. I have been seeding the idea of a master demon gadgeteer. One player was successful with creation of his exploited Hell Fire Rifle but it lead to some trouble. </div> </div> </div>Sounds solid so far. Is there a direct line of acquisition between the gadget's maker and the PC? How did they get the other component/where did it come from? Was it made with Suborned Infrastructure? (Was it <i>found</i> in Infrastructure?) Was it borrowed or stolen from another demon who made it with a specific purpose in mind?<br /> <br /> A first-order lambda may not be quite on the scale of the Dreaming Machine, but when dealing with the closest thing techgnostic espionage has to <i>storied artifacts</i> it's helpful to be able to track the history of a gadget potent enough for its aetheric resonance to be detected from a block away by the weakest of demons in the absence of protective shielding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tentative ideas<br /> Ripple : Resonant Dagger - A lethal sonic dagger that cuts like a chainsaw. Which triggers its ripple effect on the damaged caused with the dagger only.<br /> Break the Dam : Vampiric Tongue - A short sword that hungers for the blood, when triggers inflicts additional damage by sucking out the blood. </div> </div> </div>Seems solid, though a lambda with a full-sized short sword as a component must necessarily be at least that big, which takes the initial proposal of &quot;strange anime sword hilt&quot; out of consideration unless it's a really big hilt.<br /> <br /> What kind of triggers did these things have? Are there any general parameters that carried over to the lambda? Is this a &quot;simple&quot; lambda with only a novel combined effect or does it retain the powers of its components?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-18T11:43:54-07:00","id":1553256,"title":"","content":"I spoke to the player about the situation. I created these<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Resonant Dagger (Ripple Precision Engineered Embedded Gadget)</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Resonant Dagger is a simple and extremely dangerous dagger. Forged from Beryllium Copper, the sword seems to glow with a warm sunset light,etched with wavy, curving, angelic, circuitry-script. </b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Activation and Triggers: (Reflexive) To activate the dagger there is a switch in the handle that changes the line of script on the handle. Once ready, a simple tap on a hard surface causes the dagger to ring like a chime and remains this way, until the dagger hilt is untwisted.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Effect: When activated the blade becomes an incredibly efficient damaging weapon. Targets who receive damage from the blade are infused with destructive sonic energy. When the target next moves, this energy bursts forth inflicting additional damage. Half of any damage (round down) +1 inflicted by an attack of the Resonant Dagger at the beginning of the target\u2019s next action. </b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>(eg. Thomas strikes a monster with Resonant Dagger inflicting 5 points of lethal damage. On the monster\u2019s next action, the power of the dagger triggers inflicting 3 points of additional lethal damage 5/2 (round down) 2+1 = 3.)</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Resonant Dagger </b><br /> <br /> <b>Damage +1 Initiative 0 Strength 1 Size 1 8-again Enhance: Crafts or Survival</b><br /> <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Vampiric Tongue (Break the Dam Exploited Gadget)</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Vampiric Tongue is a dangerous gadget. Shaped like a dark, hollow, metallic, ice-pick, with a three sharp thread like that on a screw edged in silver-white. The blade is sharp and has a wicked hungry edge to it. </b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Activation and Triggers: (Reflexive) The weapon hungers for blood and fluids. Whenever the weapon strikes a target, the wielder flicks a switch hidden in the crossguard of the blade. </b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Effect: After striking a target, the wielder makes a Presence + Medicine + 3 - target\u2019s Stamina. Each success inflicts an additional point of lethal damage, as the blade draws out the blood of the target and into the hollow. Unfortunately Vampiric Tongue has no effect on targets without blood. </b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Vampiric Tongue</b><br /> <br /> <b>Damage +2 Initiative 0 Strength 1 Size 1</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>---</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Obscuring Clouds (Lamba - Resonant Blade &amp; Vampiric Tongue)</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Created to be a powerful weapon in the hands of the Unchained, this beautiful and deadly lambda controls the moisture in the air and turns it into a weapon. The lambda looks like the hilt of a sword made with 3 intertwined streams of metal, one obsidian black, one silver and the last copper red. At the bottom of the hilt, the 3 streams of metal flow and form into a Dara Knot with 4 stones in different shades of blue at the center of each quadrant of the knot. </b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Activation and Triggers: Instant. The wielder can activate the Lambda by sliding the 4 stones towards the center of the Knot. Moisture is pulled from the air forging the deadly weapon. This weapon can take 1 of 4 forms depending on the configuration of the stones.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Effect: In the Lambda\u2019s default form the Obscuring Clouds can be used like a Sap. Once activated, the blade of the weapon pulls moisture from the air and forms a white, misty, edge that functions and cuts just like steel. Due to the light weight nature of the weapon the strength requirement and initiative penalty to properly wield the weapon is reduced by 1. </b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hilt Damage +0 Initiative \u20130 Strength 1 Size 1</b><br /> <br /> <b>Knife Damage +1 Initiative \u20130 Strength 1 Size 2 </b><br /> <br /> <b>Katana Damage +3 Initiative \u20131 Strength 1 Size 3</b><br /> <br /> <b>Great Sword Damage +4 Initiative \u20134 Strength 3 Size 3 9-again, Two-Handed</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27908-metalith","name":"metalith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}